    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): The five avayavas re-listed as category 7 — why repeat 1.1.1's enunciation? Because there it was uddesa (naming among sixteen), here paribhasa-entry into definition-territory: each member will now receive its laksana (1.1.33-39). Order is fixed and functional: pratijna states the burden, hetu supplies ground, udaharana displays concomitance, upanaya applies it, nigamana harvests the proved. Skipping, scrambling, adding, or doubling members breaks the single-sentence bearing (ekavakyata) and incurs defeat (nyuna/adhika/anukta defects previewing 5.2's nigrahasthanas).\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Five vs three — the stock controversy (Mimamsa-Aristotelian three: proposition-reason-example?). Uddyotakara's reply: three suffice for self-inference (svartha: the thinker needs no application spelled out), five are necessary for other-inference (parartha: the opponent must be LED from his doubt through display to application to restatement). Dropping upanaya leaves hetu unjoined to subject; dropping nigamana leaves fruit unstated — the opponent nods mid-way and dissents at close. Number follows purpose: convince another, use five.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Avayava' (limb) proves the reasoning is one body (nyaya-sarira): limbs severally incomplete, jointly alive — as hands without torso grasp nothing. Each member's necessity tested by ablation: remove pratijna, direction lost; hetu, ground lost; udaharana, concomitance unshown; upanaya, joining lost; nigamana, harvest lost. The body-metaphor also explains 1.1.1's parama-nyaya praise: five-limbed reasoning is supreme among reasonings as the whole-bodied among torsos.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Parartha-structure universalized — every member corresponds to a cognitive stage in the OPPONENT (doubt, ground-seeking, concomitance-sight, self-application, assent), so the five track persuasion-psychology, not mere logic-chopping. Udayana previews hetvabhasa-mapping: each fallacy (1.2.4-9) is definable as the corruption of one member (viruddha corrupts hetu, siddha-sadhana corrupts udaharana's admittance, kalatita mistimes upanaya) — members are thus also the diagnostic grid for fallacies.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies avayava-list with pancavayava-samplava (each member embodying one pramana, 1.1.1's synthesis) and with 1.2's vada-requirement (pancavayavopapanna as debate-validity condition) — the same five serving metaphysics, epistemology, and procedure. PANINI: avayava = ava-yu + ... (limb, that which is joined-off into the whole); pratijna = prati-jna + ... (counter-knowing, declaration); hetu = hi + ... (impeller, reason); udaharana = ud-a-hr + ... (lifting-up for show); upanaya = upa-ni + ... (leading-near, application); nigamana = ni-gam + ... (leading-to-close, conclusion).",
