    "translation": "The Reason (Hetu) is the means for establishing what is to be established, derived from the similarity of the case in hand to the example.",
    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): Hetu is sadhya-sadhanam — the accomplisher of the sadhya — through udaharana-sadharmya (similarity to the example): 'because it has smoke, as the kitchen'. The hetu-property (smoke) known to coexist with the sadhya-property (fire) in the example is cognized on the subject (hill), and through that concomitance-memory the sadhya is established. 'Sadhana' marks instrumentality: hetu proves as axe cuts, not as desirer wishes.\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Two conditions unpacked — vyapti (invariable concomitance: smoke never without fire, grasped in kitchen-series) and paksadharmata (the hetu's presence on the subject: smoke seen ON this hill). Sadharmya alone without vyapti is jati (mere likeness, 1.2.18); vyapti without paksadharmata proves nothing here (kitchen-fire proves no lake). Against Dignaga's trairupya-restriction (hetu must show all three forms, excluding reasonings he dislikes): Uddyotakara accepts the three (paksadharmata, sapaksa-sattva, vipaksa-asattva) as entailed by sadharmya-through-example — the example just IS the sapaksa display, its absence-display the vipaksa — while rejecting exclusions that would banish kevala-anvayi/kevala-vyatireki (see 1.1.35 and our anvaya-vyatireki entry).\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Sadharmya' is relevant-property sameness (hetu-property possessing), not total resemblance — hill need not brick-oven-likeness, only smoke-possession like kitchen. 'Sadhana' is karana (operative instrument), distinguishing hetu from jnapaka-matra (mere indicator like a pointing finger): hetu OPERATES the cognition through concomitance, not merely occasions it.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Gamakatva (pointing-power) conditions formalized — hetu points to sadhya iff (i) anvaya-vyapti holds, (ii) hetu is paksa-present, (iii) no bhadhaka (sublating pramana) or satpratipaksa (counter-hetu) intervenes. Udayana's sighatara: hetu must be jnata (known to the audience) — unknown smoke convinces none, which is why example-display precedes hetu-use in persuasion order though hetu precedes logically.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies hetu with anumana-membership (reason embodies inference, 1.1.1's synthesis) and with 1.2.4-9's hetvabhasa-grid (each fallacy is hetu failing one condition: savyabhicara fails vyapti, asiddha fails paksadharmata, viruddha inverts pervasion). PANINI: hetu = hi + ... (impeller, that which sets cognition moving); sadhana = sadh + ... (accomplishing instrument); sadharmya = sa-dharma + ... (same-property-ness); udaharana = example (see 1.1.36).",
