    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): Udaharana is the drstanta DEPLOYED — 'whatever has smoke has fire, as the kitchen' — a familiar locus which through sadhya-sadharmya (likeness to the subject in the relevant respect) is tad-dharma-bhavi (possessed of the sadhya-property, fire-with-smoke). Two functions fused: displaying the universal (vyapti-pradarsana: where-smoke-there-fire seen) and lending it to the subject (subject is kitchen-like in smoking). Without tad-dharma-bhavitva the example is a dud (citing a smokeless oven proves nothing).\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Against the charge that udaharana merely repeats drstanta (1.1.25): drstanta is the admitted STOCK (kitchen agreed to contain fire-smoke), udaharana its CITATION inside proof with the universal made explicit ('whatever...'). Stock without citation convinces none; citation without admitted stock proves nothing — hence separate category (there) and member (here). Against the three-membered (omit example as redundant once hetu stated): hetu states concomitance CLAIMED, example shows it SEEN — claim without show persuades only the already-convinced.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Sadhya-sadharmyat' fenced as hetu-property likeness (smoke-possession), not sadhya-identity (the kitchen need not be THE hill, need not share altitude) — else no example could ever illustrate (nothing duplicates the subject). 'Tad-dharma-bhavi' requires actual possession, not repute: a rumoured-fiery kitchen nobody verified is no udaharana; admittance (drstanta-status) is presupposed, linking 1.1.25's agreement-condition into proof's heart.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Udaharana as vyapti-smaraka (remembrancer of concomitance): its psychological office is triggering the hearer's latent universal ('oh yes, smoke-fire together always') at the decisive moment before application. Udayana grades examples — prasiddha (kitchen, best), sastra-prasiddha (scriptural, for adrsta topics), yukta-kalpita (constructed, weakest, allowed only where no stock exists) — all valid iff admitted by both parties.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies udaharana with pratyaksa-membership (example embodies perception, 1.1.1's synthesis) and with 1.1.36-37 pairing (positive display needs negative twin, else accidental co-presence suspected) — the member that LOOKS most dispensable is the proof's eyes. PANINI: udaharana = ud-a-hr + ... (lifting-up for show, illustration); drstanta = settled instance (see 1.1.25); bhavin = bhu + ... (possessing, being-endowed).",
