    "translation": "Or, through its dissimilarity, it is destitute of that property.",
    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): The negative example (vaidharmya-drstanta) — 'whatever lacks fire lacks smoke, as the lake' — tadviparyayat (through contrariety to that positive case), viparitam (the reverse exhibit): destitute of the sadhya-property precisely as destitute of hetu-property. The lake, unlike hill-kitchen in smoking, is fireless — displaying vyatireka-vyapti (fire-absence to smoke-absence) the way the kitchen displayed anvaya.\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): 'Va' (or) marks optionality with parity: EITHER positive example alone (where negative unavailable, as in some kevala-anvayi reasonings) OR negative alone (kevala-vyatireki) OR both (standard anvaya-vyatireki) — validity tracks vyapti-grasp, not example-count. Against example-skeptics (no locus is purely fireless — lake has submarine fire? fisherman's hearth?): purity is relative to the hetu-sadhya pair (lake lacks hill-relevant fire-smoke conjunction), not absolute sterility — else no negative example could ever exist and vyatireka would be unshowable.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Tadviparyayat' fenced as contrariety to the POSITIVE concomitance (anvaya), not contrariety to the subject (hill-lake differences in size, wetness are irrelevant) — the reverse must mirror the same two properties negated. 'Viparita' as property-absent exhibit: the lake's firelessness must be ADMITTED (drstanta-grade), not itself doubtful, else the illustration begs — negative examples need admittance exactly as positive ones do.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Negative display completes induction against accidental co-presence: smoke-fire co-occurrence in kitchens could be coincidence (both effects of cooking-activity?) — their joint ABSENCE in lakes, where cooking is absent, rules out common-cause accident and confirms pervasion. Udayana's sighatara: negative examples persuade doubters of universality ('all' claims) more than positives, since one admitted absence breaks the counterexample-search.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies 1.1.37 with 1.1.35 (negative hetu needs negative display) and 1.2.18's jati-warning (mere dissimilarity-citing without vyapti is futility) — legitimate vyatireka-display distinguished from jati-chatter by admitted concomitance-absence. PANINI: viparyaya = vi-pari-i + ... (going-against-around, contrariety); viparita = vi-pari-i + ... (reversed, contrary-exhibited); va = ... (or, option-marker).",
