    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): Vitanda is SAH (that jalpa) pratipaksa-sthapana-hina — devoid of counter-thesis establishment. The vitandika attacks ('sound is not proved non-eternal by your reason') while asserting nothing ('I claim neither eternal nor non-eternal'). Pure refutation without position: demolition crew with no construction plan. Lowest of the three because truth-indifferent by structure — even successful vitanda yields only the opponent's failure, never any truth.\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Does the vitandika IMPLICITLY hold the negation (denying non-eternal = asserting eternal)? No — undertaking (parigraha) differs from implication: he undertakes NO proof-burden (bhara-hina), so no thesis can be imputed however his denials sound. Consequence: vitanda can never WIN positively, only PREVENT the opponent's win — bouts end in frustration/draw unless the opponent self-defeats (nigrahasthana by his own fault). Still enumerated because sophists infest assemblies practicing it; recognizing the form lets umpires name it and deny it victor's laurels. Defensive legitimacy: against deniers-of-all-pramanas (who assert 'no proof proves'), refutation-without-thesis is the ONLY possible reply — displaying their denial's self-defeat ('your denial proves nothing, so why trust it?') needs no counter-thesis.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Sthapana' is establishment-WITH-proof (pramana-backed), not mere utterance — the vitandika may UTTER sentences ('your hetu deviates') while establishing NOTHING, since demolishing another's proof proves no rival. 'Hina' (devoid) is structural, not accidental: jalpa minus sthapana by DEFINITION, so no vitanda can graduate into jalpa mid-bout by suddenly proving — that would be starting a new debate, judged afresh.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Vitanda's prayojana dissected — obstruction (pratibandha), fame-through-demolition (khyati), patron-pleasing (paritosana): all person-serving, none truth-serving. Hence lowest rank is structural, not moralizing: a form whose success-conditions exclude truth cannot serve tattva even accidentally. Udayana's test: ask the vitandika 'what should the assembly BELIEVE after your victory?' — silence (or 'nothing') confesses the void.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies vitanda with 1.1.1's katha-traya (third form, positionless) and 5.2's nigrahasthana-table (vitanda-practitioners incur defeat the moment they smuggle a thesis — sthapana-hina violated by their own mouths). PANINI: vitanda = vi-tand + ... (destructive wrangling, tearing apart); sthapana = stha + ... (establishing, setting up); hina = ha + ... (abandoned, devoid of).",
