    "translation": "The contradictory reason (Viruddha) is one which opposes an established tenet.",
    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): Viruddha is siddhantam abhyupetya tadvirodhi — having undertaken a tenet, opposing it by one's own hetu: undertaking 'sound is non-eternal' then adducing 'because eternal' (or undertaking eternality then adducing 'because produced'). The hetu pervades the vipaksa (produced-ness pervades non-eternality), so it proves the CONTRARY of the thesis — worse than proving nothing, it proves the opponent's case with one's own mouth.\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Two readings fenced — (i) siddhanta as the proponent's OWN pratijna-tenet (undertaken in this debate): hetu contradicting it is self-defeat; (ii) siddhanta as the school's prati-tantra tenet: hetu contradicting it is party-treason (proving what one's school denies). Both incur defeat, differently: (i) is pratijna-virodha (thesis-contradiction, 5.2), (ii) is siddhanta-virodha proper. Against conflation with savyabhicara: the erratic proves NEITHER end (inconclusive), viruddha proves THE OTHER end (decisive-against) — mistaking them mistreats refuted as merely doubtful.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Abhyupetya' (having undertaken) is load-bearing — viruddha requires PRIOR undertaking; a hetu merely inconsistent with unundertaken truths is not viruddha but possibly sound (proving the surprising). 'Tadvirodhi' is hetu-anking toward vipaksa: the hetu must be vipaksa-vyapta (pervading the counter-locus), not merely vipaksa-present (that is savyabhicara's ordinary form) — pervasion decides, presence merely suspects.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Vipaksa-vyapti formalized — hetu H is viruddha for sadhya S iff (H → not-S) holds with the same strictness demanded of valid vyapti (H → S): contradiction borrows validity's own machinery to hang the thesis. Udayana's sighatara: viruddha needs no vipaksa-search (unlike savyabhicara's suspicion-procedure) — one glance at pervasion-direction suffices: does this hetu LIVE in the counter-locus essentially? Produced-ness lives in non-eternity essentially — instant verdict.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies viruddha with hetu-condition two inverted (direction, not pervasion, fails) and with 5.2's pratijna-virodha nigrahasthana (self-contradiction as debate-death) — the fallacy that kills its user first. PANINI: viruddha = vi-rudh + ... (obstructed-opposite, set-against); abhyupetya = abhi-upa-i + ... (having undertaken, gone-near to accept); virodhin = vi-rudh + ... (opposing).",
