    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): Prakaranasama is yasmāt prakaranacinta — that from which the inquiry's anxiety persists: nirnayartham apadista (adduced for deciding) yet leaving prakarana (the question) in original doubt. Stock case: 'sound is non-eternal because not possessing eternality's marks' — restating non-eternality as its own proof, so eternal-vs-not stands exactly where it stood. Begging dressed as proving: the hetu IS the sadhya reworded, provoking the same cinta it was hired to settle.\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Symmetrical-rival analysis — prakaranasama bites hardest where BOTH sides wield apparent hetus (eternalists: 'sound eternal because intangible'; non-eternalists: 'sound non-eternal because produced'), each leaving the other unmoved; the offered hetu cannot DECIDE because an equal-and-opposite stands. Distinguished from savyabhicara (deviation across loci) and sadhyasama (unproved base): here base may be granted, pervasion may hold somewhere — the fault is INDECISION between poised rivals, not deviation or absence. Cure is visesa (differentiator): fresh ground breaking symmetry (produced-ness has no eternalist answer, while intangibility does) — tarka or decisive example must intervene.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Prakarana' is the live question (prastuta-vicara), 'cinta' its anxiety-tension; 'sama' (equal) means leaving the question in EQUAL doubt-posture — neither advancing nor retreating it. Vacaspati fences prakaranasama from siddha-sadhana (proving the admitted: wasteful but harmless) — prakaranasama is worse, proving the DISPUTED by itself, actively immunizing doubt against cure.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Indecision formalized — hetu H is prakaranasama iff rival hetu H' for not-S stands undefeated alongside: proof-parity, not proof-absence, is the fault. Udayana's sighatara: prakaranasama needs RIVAL-SEARCH (unlike savyabhicara's vipaksa-search): produce the counter-hetu to convict. Resolution hierarchy: visesa (differentiating ground) > tarka (absurdity of rival) > drstanta-refresh (new decisive example) — escalating breakers of symmetry.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies prakaranasama with 2.1's doubt-defence (the no-doubt objector's 'equal conviction' charge is prakaranasama-licence: mistaking balanced hetus for doubt's impossibility) and with 5.2's tulya-nigrahasthana (parity-pleading as defeat-condition) — the fallacy that weaponizes balance. PANINI: prakaranasama = prakarana + sama (equal to the question); cinta = cit + ... (anxious thought); nirnayartham = nirnaya + artham (for the sake of deciding).",
