    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): The objector collapses upacara into vak — vaka chhalam eva upacara-chhalam, tat avisesat (metaphor-quibble just IS term-quibble, from non-difference): both impose an artha-antara (alternative meaning) on the speaker's words, differing in no relevant respect. If genus holds (alternative-imposition), species-division is inflation — two names, one trick. The charge threatens 1.2.11's restrictive three: prove no difference, and three shrink to two (or one).\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Sharpens into genus-species logic — IF the differentia (upacara vs slesa) is unreal, THEN the species collapse; the objector claims the only common feature (alternative-meaning) exhausts both, leaving no differentiating remainder. Uddyotakara stages the dispute honestly: MANY futile rejoinders indeed ignore example-similarity (the p.609 footnote's point — jati need not involve examples), so 'similarity/dissimilarity to example' language is illustrative (nidarsana-matra), not exhaustive — similarly here, 'alternative meaning' may ILLUSTRATE both quibbles without EXHAUSTING either, leaving room for Gautama's replies (1.2.16-17) to exhibit the remainder.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Avisesat' (from non-difference) fenced as absence of RELEVANT difference — the objector concedes surface differences (homonym vs figure) but deems them irrelevant to quibble-hood, as colour-differences are irrelevant to pot-hood. The reply-burden is thus fixed: exhibit a difference RELEVANT to quibble-mechanics (how the trick works), not any difference (what words are involved) — a burden 1.2.16 discharges via artha-antara-bhava (differing alternative-STATUS).\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Collapse-arguments generalized — same form attacks samanya too ('all three impose alternatives, so one chhala'): the objector's logic proves too much, erasing even his own footing (if all is one, his 'two' collapses to one as well — self-devouring objection). Udayana's sighatara: collapse needs EXHAUSTION-proof (alternative-meaning exhausts both species with no remainder); exhibiting any functional remainder (homonym-dependence vs transfer-dependence) defeats it — remainder defeats reduction.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies the objection with 1.2.11's promise (division made) and 1.2.16-17's replies (division defended) — objection as middle panel of the triptych (enumerate, object, defend). PANINI: avisesat = a-vi-sesa + ... (ablative: from/because of non-difference); eva = ... (just, exactly — identity-marker); vaka-chhalam eva (term-quibble JUST).",
