    "commentary": "BHASYA (Vatsyayana): Tad-vikalpat (from THEIR variety) jati-nigrahasthana-bahutvam (the multiplicity of futility and defeat): because jati ramifies (24 in Book 5: sadharana-varieties, time-place-predicate tableaux) and nigrahasthana ramifies (22: pratijna-virodha through matanujna), the two are declared manifold HERE by anticipation. 'Vikalpa' (variety) is not doubt here but ramification — one genus, many species, each needing its own diagnosis and cure.\n\nVARTIKA (Uddyotakara): Against the charge of promissory enumeration (declaring multiplicity without displaying it — empty bahutva): anticipation is legitimate where the genus-definition already contains the branching principle — jati's tableaux-principle (vary the tableau, new jati) and nigraha's duty-breach principle (vary the duty, new defeat) GENERATE their species deductively, so bahutva is proved though instances await Book 5. Against demanding full anatomy now: Adhyaya 1 is uddesa-laksana (mention-definition); pariksa-anatomy belongs to Books 2-5 by trividha-sastra-pravrtti division of labour — premature anatomy would break the sastra's own method.\n\nTATPARYA (Vacaspati): 'Tad' (their) fenced as jati-nigrahasthana specifically (not all sixteen): only these two multiply WITHOUT new ontological cost — vikalpa here is combinatorial (tableaux × duties), not creative (no new realities posited). Hence bahutva enriches debate-taxonomy while ontology stays at sixteen: method ramifies, being does not. The colophon-function: 1.2.20 closes Adhyaya 1 exactly as 1.2.17 closed chhala (plurality vindicated as method) — multiplicity-from-variety is the treatise's signature move.\n\nPARISUDDHI (Udayana): Multiplicity formalized — J = {tableaux T × vyapti-neglect} (24 = exhibited subset, extendable: any new tableau neglecting pervasion JOINS jati by definition, so the list is open-textured, not closed); N = {duties D × breach-modes} (22 = exhibited subset, same open texture). Udayana's sighatara: jati/nigraha membership is DEFINITIONAL (satisfy formula, join kind) not enumerative (listed, therefore member) — new tricks (printing-press quibbles? telegraph-literalisms?) join automatically. The sutra thus legislates for futures, not just pasts.\n\nBHASHYACHANDRA (Raghuttama): Tallies the colophon — 'thus have pramana and the rest been mentioned and defined; examination will follow' (Jha p.584) — with 1.1.1's promise (tattvajnana → nihsreyasa) and Adhyaya 1's four achievements ((a) theme, (b) metempsychosis-process, (c) cessation-by-knowledge, (d) mention-definition of categories): promise mapped, ground surveyed, tools sharpened — Books 2-5 may now examine. 'Thus ends Adhyaya 1 of Uddyotakara's Vartika on the Nyaya-Bhasya.' PANINI: bahutva = bahu + ... (manifoldness, multiplicity); vikalpa = vi-klp + ... (variety, ramification); tad = ... (their, of those two).",
